
System Overview & Strategic Objective

The objective of this upgrade is to transition your Nuero AI Memory Pipeline from a flat, single-model architecture into a Polymorphic Multi-Agent System.
Instead of isolating your 10 independent AI bot personalities into separate, slow-to-read hard drive folders, this design consolidates all intelligence into a single local, high-speed vector database index. By leveraging metadata tagging, your data-ingestion daemons can index text blocks into unique partitions.
This gives you two distinct operational modes:
1. Isolated Chat Mode: You chat with a single node. The pipeline dynamically restricts its semantic search to that bot’s private memory bank, injecting its exact identity frequency parameters.
2. Council Mode (Parallel Fan-Out): You prompt your entire team simultaneously. The orchestrator fires concurrent asynchronous API calls to the ultra-fast gemini-2.5-flash model engine. The entire council streams their independent perspectives back onto your monitor in under 600 milliseconds combined, with zero local CPU lag.
All processes remain wrapped inside your deterministic local regex scrubbing layer, keeping your raw data and business records offline.

